Q: string() function doesn&#39;t work in document.evaluate A: <pre><code>document.evaluate(&quot;string(//@id)&quot;, document, null, XPathResult.STRING_TYPE, null)
</code></pre>
<p>Replace <code>ORDERED_NODE_SNAPSHOT_TYPE</code> with <code>XPathResult.STRING_TYPE</code>, since <code>string()</code> returns a string, not a node-set. Then get the value using <code>.stringValue</code>:</p>
<pre><code>const result = document.evaluate(&quot;string(//@id)&quot;, document, null, XPathResult.STRING_TYPE, null);

console.log(result.stringValue);
</code></pre>

